  "docs.s.deal-scores.title": "How deal scores work",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.summary": "Scores compare asking price to a market median — Good Deal, Fair, or Overpriced.",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.body.0": "A deal score answers one question: is this asking price cheap, fair, or rich versus peers? The core formula is score = (1 − price / median) × 100. Positive scores mean under-median; negative scores mean over-median.",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.body.1": "Bands align with the deal ladder used across the app: Good Deal when score ≥ 8 (about 8% or more under median), Overpriced when score ≤ −5 (about 5% or more over median), and Fair otherwise. Medians are built from recent comparable listings — same lane where possible, with district and condition context when sample depth allows.",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.body.2": "Treat strong scores with thin samples as provisional. Always check freshness, peer count, and district mix before you treat a score as a negotiation floor. Best Picks ranks listings that clear both score and confidence thresholds.",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.bullet.0": "Good Deal: score ≥ 8 (asking ≤ ~92% of median)",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.bullet.1": "Fair: between the Good Deal and Overpriced bands",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.bullet.2": "Overpriced: score ≤ −5 (asking ≥ ~105% of median)",
  "docs.s.deal-scores.bullet.3": "Confidence rises with sample size and fresh comps",
  "docs.s.official-pulse.title": "Official Pulse",
